    "rationale": "Fix for round 1: overwriting all five N-blocks onto accumulator rows 0-15 destroyed four blocks before mvout. Since 32 accumulator rows can hold only two pending 16-row N-block results, N=80 is processed in three groups {0,1},{2,3},{4}. Per group: with A K-chunk 0 resident in scratchpad rows 0-15, compute both blocks' K-chunk 0 in overwrite mode (block j into acc rows 0-15, block j+1 into acc rows 16-31); then load A K-chunk 1 into rows 0-15 and compute both blocks' K-chunk 1 in accumulate mode onto the same rows, yielding reductions in increasing K order; then mvout both blocks to C element offsets j*16 with store stride 320 bytes. Every B tile (2 K-steps x 5 N-blocks) is DMA'd exactly once (10 tiles); A chunks are loaded once per group (3x2 = 6 tiles) since K-chunk 0 and K-chunk 1 computes cannot overlap in the 32-row scratchpad (rows 0-15 A tile, rows 16-31 B tile). Total 16 mvin tiles = 4096 input bytes, the minimum given the accumulator-residency constraint; all computes use accumulated=false with preload-staged B tiles, bd_spad_addr is always GARBAGE_ADDR, and every out_addr/acc_addr sets bit 31 (accumulator) and bit 29 (full C width), with bit 30 distinguishing accumulate (3758096384/3758096400) from overwrite (2684354560/2684354576)."
